<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">3 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 3 October, from 382 to 1990.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">382 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,644 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Theodosius I settles the Goths inside the Roman Empire</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperor Theodosius I concluded a treaty allowing the Goths to settle south of the Danube as semi-autonomous allies. Giving a whole people land within the frontier set a precedent that reshaped the late Roman world.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodosius-i">Theodosius I</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1226 CE <span class="tih-ago">800 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Francis of Assisi dies at the Porziuncola</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Francis of Assisi died at the Porziuncola chapel below Assisi. The merchant's son who embraced radical poverty had founded the Franciscan order, and he was canonised less than two years later.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1863 CE <span class="tih-ago">163 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lincoln proclaims a national day of Thanksgiving</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Amid the Civil War, Abraham Lincoln proclaimed the last Thursday of November a national day of thanksgiving. The proclamation answered years of campaigning by the editor Sarah Josepha Hale and began an annual federal holiday.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1929 CE <span class="tih-ago">97 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">King Alexander renames his realm the Kingdom of Yugoslavia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Alexander I renamed the Kingdom of Serbs, Croats and Slovenes as Yugoslavia, 'land of the South Slavs', as part of his royal dictatorship. The new name was meant to override the national rivalries dividing the state.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenes">Slovenes</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croats">Croats</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1990 CE <span class="tih-ago">36 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Germany is reunified</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The German Democratic Republic acceded to the Federal Republic, reuniting Germany 45 years after its division. The peaceful merger, less than a year after the Berlin Wall opened, marked the close of the Cold War in Europe.</p></div></li></ol>
